WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.604
[ Heart beating ]

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.973
-Cut!
Everyone, just take five.

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:09.442
-I'm sorry about that last take.
-What the [bleep] is going on?

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.677
-I'm just a little out of it.
-Are you on drugs?

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:14.046
Don't [bleep] lie to me.

00:00:14.046 --> 00:00:15.714
This has been going on
for a while now.

00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:17.650
This has got to stop.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.051
I don't know who
you're hanging out with,

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:22.054
but on my set,
nobody does drugs, all right?

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:23.356
That includes my actors.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:27.059
Come back in a half-hour
ready to work.

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:30.196
Just --
You're 18 now, man.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.664
Don't [bleep] it up.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:33.733
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Chris Kattan.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:37.137
That was a clip from "Famous."
Tell us a bit about it.

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:39.906
-It's a --
Well, it's a really good movie,

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:42.308
and, you know,
I'm happy to be in it,

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:45.845
and I chose to be in it, not
just because I got to do drama,

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.914
which I like doing,
but Michael Leoni,

00:00:48.914 --> 00:00:50.817
who's the director,
had a great vision.

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:53.520
It was based on a play
that he directed,

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.521
and this play --

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:57.456
Well, the movie has
the same actors in the play.

00:00:57.456 --> 00:01:01.661
So, when I got on board,
his vision was so strong

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:04.230
and powerful that I was like,
"Oh, my God.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.232
I love being part of this,"
you know?

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.968
And I took a chance, and I'm
really happy I was in it.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.337
-It's great
to see you doing drama.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.873
It's also very exciting
that you're doing sketch again.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.475
You have a YouTube sketch show

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:16.876
where you're doing
a new sketch every week.

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:20.246
-Yes.
It's called "Hey, Kattan."

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.114
-How did you come up with
the name "Hey, Kattan"?

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:23.449
-Whoo!
-Thank you.

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:28.354
-So, somebody on the street
said, "Hey, Kattan!"

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:29.655
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.655 --> 00:01:32.258
Well, most people acknowledge me
by saying, "Hey, Kattan."

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.894
They don't go, "Hey, Chris,"
or, "Hey, Chris Kattan."

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.529
-You've always been a Kattan.
-Or, "Hey, Chris Kattan.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.264
I heard that Seth Meyers
and his wife

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.767
met at your wedding, period."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.735
-Period, end of story.
-End of story.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:47.273
But, no, yeah.
So, it's a great opportunity

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.507
for me to write, you know?

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:51.243
And I get
to direct these shorts.

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:54.313
-Do impressions again?
-Do impressions.

00:01:54.313 --> 00:01:57.550
My classic Harrison Ford.
-Harrison Ford.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.285
-Who could forget
my Harrison Ford?

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.186
-Not a lot of people can do
a good Harrison Ford.

00:02:01.186 --> 00:02:03.223
-No.
[ Laughs ]

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:06.091
Here's my --
Oh, I actually met him.

00:02:06.091 --> 00:02:08.194
Well, a few times.
The first time I met him,

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:11.063
I was so excited to meet him
that I was like, "Oh, my God!

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:13.132
You're Harrison Ford!
I'm so excited!

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.668
I feel like Short Round!"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:16.802
That's what I said.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:18.671
-'Cause I was that excited.
-Sure, sure.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.740
-Can we say short round?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:24.010
-And he said...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:28.214
I'll hold on that laugh 'cause
you chose to laugh at that.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:31.217
So, but he --
I said, "I'm so excited.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.620
I feel like Short Round."
He went, "Settle."

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.288
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.423
And then, I saw him again
at a dentist office,

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:39.258
and I said,
"Hey, Harrison Ford --"

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:41.627
I don't know why I'm screaming,
but I did scream at the time.

00:02:41.627 --> 00:02:42.861
That's how I get excited.
-Yeah.

00:02:42.861 --> 00:02:44.363
"Hey, Harrison Ford!
It's me!

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:47.333
Remember me, Chris Kattan?"
He went, "Settle," again.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.803
So every time I see him,
he goes, "Settle."

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.271
-Yeah.
-The third time,

00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:54.440
he said, "Settle."
-Well, I mean, the third time,

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.808
you're lucky
he didn't call the cops.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:57.443
-Yeah, that's right!
-Yeah.

00:02:57.443 --> 00:03:00.813
-"Settle."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:04.116
That would've been -- yeah.
But I hear you do an impre--

00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:06.419
We did --
Oh, this is another thing

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:08.855
you can take account
that I helped you with, maybe.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.089
I don't know.
-Yeah.

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:15.094
-But was on "SNL,"
you did a Hugh Grant impression.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:18.198
-In one of my first "SNLs,"
you put me in a Mango

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:19.899
with Gwyneth Paltrow,
and there I am

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:22.234
doing Hugh Grant right there.
-There you go.

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:25.104
-So, I don't know if you know,
but, like, on "SNL,"

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:27.240
When you first get on the show,
you're like, "Oh, I'd like

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.041
to get in the --"
You know, get some air time,

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:31.277
as they say, or whatever.
And you're obviously talented,

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:34.280
and you did an amazing --
-Kind of threw that off...

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.481
-Yeah, exactly, I said,
"Oh, my God!

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:38.450
What an amazing
Hugh Grant impression!"

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.619
And so there you are
doing Hugh Grant.

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:42.288
And you went...
[ Gibberish ]

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.756
-Yeah, yeah.
That was basically it.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:44.923
That's all I had.
-Yeah.

00:03:44.923 --> 00:03:46.593
-That and I, like,
looked like him.

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:48.227
-Well, it's better
than my, "Settle."

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:49.962
-No, the "settle's" good.
-Oh, it is good?

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:53.032
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
But I started going to

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.467
impression camp, and I'm very
good at impressions now.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.902
-Impression camp?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:58.070
I went to a camp.
I went to an intensive camp.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.005
-For impressions.
-For impressions, yeah.

00:04:00.005 --> 00:04:02.842
-I don't know if I like that.
-Oh, no.

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.644
You don't like it
when you're there.

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.045
It's very intense.
-You walk in,

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.347
and everybody's doing
different impressions?

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:09.682
-Yeah!
-"Hey, oh..."

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.550
I don't want to name out
what you just did,

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.286
but I'm a little confused
it's a camp.

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:14.487
-Yeah, but I went,
and it went great.

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:17.390
And I never --
You always had a great Pacino,

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.392
and now I have
a passable Al Pacino.

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:22.361
-Oh. Can I see --
Well, my Pacino --

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:23.730
-You do yours first.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.631
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:28.368
-Is this how you are at camp?
-Well, no.

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.870
At the end --
-"You do yours first."

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:34.440
[ Laughter ]
So aggressive.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.409
So, I was like --
I still want to go to that camp.

00:04:37.409 --> 00:04:40.312
-Yeah, you could be a counselor.
-Why?

00:04:40.312 --> 00:04:42.815
I already went from being a guy
who does impressions

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:44.083
to a counselor?
That's so nice.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:45.518
-Yeah.
-Thank you.

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:47.286
Like, I graduated already.
-Well, but you could lose it

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:49.455
on this Pacino.
-Okay. Well, hold on.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.525
So, my Pacino is basically
the blind Pacino.

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:53.626
You know,
from "Scent of a Woman."

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.728
There's different stages
of Pacinos.

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:57.697
There's the "Godfather,"
like, "I know!"

00:04:57.697 --> 00:05:01.367
That one from "The Godfather."
But then there's the "Hoo ha!"

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.202
That one.
That's the one I did.

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:05.905
So everyone loves that one.
But there's a new Pacino --

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:09.108
-Well, my Pacino started
because he was at some award.

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:10.576
And maybe -- I don't know
which award show it was.

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:12.045
He was in a Zoom room.
-Oh.

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:15.981
-And so we took great joy in
thinking about Al Pacino going

00:05:15.981 --> 00:05:18.785
like, "Al Pacino
in the Zoom room!"

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:20.519
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:22.388
"Look at me."
-That's what he did?

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.090
"Look at me."
-"I'm in a Zoom room."

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.526
-"I'm in a Zumba room."
-"I don't know what this is."

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:29.328
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:30.896
They said,
"Meet me in the Zoom room."

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:32.398
You'd get cancelled.
You can't do that impression.

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.333
-You can't do it anymore?
-Yeah, you can't do Pacino.

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:36.436
But he does a --
[ Laughs ]

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:38.671
I know he's got "House of Gucci"
movie coming out.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:42.342
So, he's Italian, he's like,
"I am -- you la puciata feta!"

00:05:42.342 --> 00:05:46.211
-Oh, is that --
-"La ta tuci, la pucci!"

00:05:46.211 --> 00:05:47.813
-Have you seen "House of Gucci"?
-No, I have not.

00:05:47.813 --> 00:05:49.982
-Oh, wow.
So, you're so confident

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:52.518
in your Al Pacino impression...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:55.154
-I went to the West Coast
Camp of Impressions.

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:57.189
-Oh, you did?
And they said,

00:05:57.189 --> 00:05:58.524
"'House of Gucci,'
just take your Pacino,

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.759
put a little Italian in it,
do it again."

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:02.694
Now that I know
what I'm listening for,

00:06:02.694 --> 00:06:04.563
do an Al Pacino
in the "House of Gucci"

00:06:04.563 --> 00:06:06.064
that you haven't seen yet.

00:06:06.064 --> 00:06:10.703
-"Oh! Uh, what-a everybody's
wearing a-here?"

00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:11.970
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:14.239
-It's very good.
-Thank you.

00:06:14.239 --> 00:06:17.543
-You guys, that's Chris Kattan.
"Famous" is in theaters

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:19.212
and available on demand
December 10th.

